# Line endings are part of this repo's contract, not a display preference.
#
# Overlay sources are mounted onto the runner and their exact sha256 is pinned
# (PREIMAGES in glm53_prep_fused.py and glm53_drafter_prep.py); launchers/ run
# under bash on the Linux boxes; deploy-overlays.sh copies working-tree bytes
# and verifies them with sha256sum. A checkout that rewrites LF to CRLF flips
# every one of those digests -- check_preimages() then reports drift and the
# overlay disarms to the stock path -- so source is never EOL-converted, on any
# platform. Without this file Git for Windows applies core.autocrlf=true from
# its system gitconfig and does exactly that.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Captured evidence and build outputs keep the bytes they were captured with.
measurements/** -text
*.log -text
*.gz -text
*.cubin -text
